1
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:20,300
ANN CONNOR: This is Tuesday, September the 13th, 1983, and this is Ann Connor.

2
00:00:20,310 --> 00:00:28,800
ANN CONNOR: I've just been over at the Miller Homestead preparing for a flower show to be given by the Bethel Garden Club, and

3
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:38,400
I took along with me the prayer that Mrs. Edna Miller Maits gave at the homestead back in 1979.

4
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:46,100
I also took some pictures of the Bicentennial with pictures of Mrs. Maits at the homestead.

5
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:59,240
I'm now headed over to Edna Croco. Tomorrow at the Women's Association meeting at Bethel Presbyterian Church I've been asked to read

6
00:00:59,240 --> 00:01:10,400
the prayer that Mrs. Maits made at the homestead, and I'm hoping to get some additional information about Edna's thoughts and memories

7
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:42,680
of Mrs. Maits, to add to that prayer.

8
00:01:42,690 --> 00:01:44,060
ANN CONNOR: I'm going to turn it on and you can hear me.

9
00:01:44,100 --> 00:01:57,900
EDNA: Well, I remember Edna Maits when she was a young girl. I was her, well, I don't know.

10
00:01:57,910 --> 00:02:09,875
I wouldn't say whether she was born over there or not, but my grandmother had property down over the hill from Johnston

11
00:02:09,875 --> 00:02:11,915
Wilson.

12
00:02:11,925 --> 00:02:13,635
ANN CONNOR: Okay. And Wilson Road. Yeah. All right.

13
00:02:13,645 --> 00:02:32,415
EDNA: And they rented that. And I remember going over there when, well, shortly after Mama died, with Daddy, to collect the rent,

14
00:02:32,415 --> 00:02:47,755
and then I got to know Edna better with getting into the white of Bible plans.

15
00:02:47,765 --> 00:02:55,115
EDNA: And she was one of the members that hung out to the end of the Bible class.

16
00:02:55,115 --> 00:03:19,975
There was Blanche McEwen and I forget who else was in there. And we used to have in that class, we used

17
00:03:19,975 --> 00:03:30,195
to have as high as 75 members, but they all died and got married, moved away.

18
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:39,655
EDNA: Well, I have a picture of Dr. Wycoff's Bible class, and one of the things that she wanted to be sure that

19
00:03:39,655 --> 00:03:47,435
we saved, that was stashed out in the barn, is that table that we have up in the historical room that she

20
00:03:47,435 --> 00:03:55,015
said he used in the Bible class as his table, where he put his books and so on.

21
00:03:55,015 --> 00:03:59,015
That was one thing she made me aware of.

22
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:02,100
ANN CONNOR: Now, you say that you lived there.

23
00:04:02,300 --> 00:04:20,555
EDNA: Well, I better not put this on the tape.

24
00:04:20,565 --> 00:04:21,065
ANN CONNOR: I was going to ask you who was going to get this bill.

25
00:04:21,075 --> 00:04:21,575
EDNA: Well, I don't know. I don't know anything about that. That's a decision that the Millers have to make.

26
00:04:21,585 --> 00:04:28,175
ANN CONNOR: But to get back to your statement that they lived over on Wilson Road: one day I took Edna for a ride

27
00:04:28,175 --> 00:04:37,575
in the car, and she pointed out a house that is on Wilson Road as you drop down past from where the

28
00:04:37,575 --> 00:04:43,115
Wilson farm was on the hill, and she said that that was where she lived as a little girl, and that she

29
00:04:43,115 --> 00:04:50,915
was born in a log house. Did you know that? And she said that the log house is gone, but the other

30
00:04:50,915 --> 00:04:54,015
house is still there.

31
00:04:54,025 --> 00:04:57,175
ANN CONNOR: Did you know that that was the case?

32
00:04:57,185 --> 00:05:01,895
EDNA: I didn't know whether she was born over there or not.

33
00:05:02,100 --> 00:05:06,975
ANN CONNOR: Well, she told us that. That's on my other tape, in the ride that I took.

34
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:10,535
EDNA: And then there was three Ednas.

35
00:05:10,545 --> 00:05:11,045
ANN CONNOR: Three Ednas?

36
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:20,935
EDNA: Yeah. And there was a man down here at the library. He was a carpenter and he built houses, and his name

37
00:05:20,935 --> 00:05:33,135
was Ross Patterson, and he had a daughter named Edna, and he was building the house over to my grandmother, or my

38
00:05:33,135 --> 00:05:41,435
grandmother Wilson's, one down over the hill, and he coached them to call her Edna.

39
00:05:41,435 --> 00:05:53,155
And then I was born in Edna Patterson, Edna Miller, and Edna Croco.

40
00:05:53,165 --> 00:05:55,695
ANN CONNOR: Yeah, three Ednas.

41
00:05:55,705 --> 00:06:08,585
EDNA: And the other Edna was, oh, Edna Simmons.

42
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:11,045
ANN CONNOR: Oh, she was one of them.

43
00:06:11,055 --> 00:06:20,225
EDNA: No, there was three. Just Edna Maits and myself and Edna Simmons.

44
00:06:21,300 --> 00:06:39,065
EDNA: And it was in 1899 when the Simmons house burnt. And Edna, Aunt Maggie, was took Ed, when they took her out,

45
00:06:39,165 --> 00:06:53,225
they told her not to look back. That was the 19th of April, and Edna was born the 19th of May.

46
00:06:54,285 --> 00:07:00,845
And they didn't want her to look back because they were afraid she would be marked.

47
00:07:00,855 --> 00:07:02,345
ANN CONNOR: Who was born?

48
00:07:02,355 --> 00:07:03,745
EDNA: Edna Simmons.

49
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:09,065
EDNA: And I'm the last of the three.

50
00:07:09,075 --> 00:07:11,185
ANN CONNOR: Edna, you're the last of the three.

51
00:07:14,400 --> 00:07:24,125
ANN CONNOR: Well, are there any things that... now, I did talk to you before about remembering when the roof fell off of the

52
00:07:24,125 --> 00:07:33,865
meeting house. I wasn't there. I wasn't there. But is there anything that you can recall that would be of interest about

53
00:07:33,865 --> 00:07:35,625
that third meeting house?

54
00:07:38,300 --> 00:07:45,665
ANN CONNOR: For instance, I have the water cooler that was used there. Now, where was that place, and who was in charge of

55
00:07:45,665 --> 00:07:47,545
filling that water, you know?

56
00:07:47,555 --> 00:07:52,625
EDNA: Well, I suppose it would be the caretaker, and that was Jacob Morlock.

57
00:07:52,635 --> 00:08:05,925
EDNA: And they got the water from the well, what you would know better, down over the hill from where the parsonage was.

58
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:24,085
ANN CONNOR: Who was in charge of flowers, for instance? You remember, you know, even just some of the details of how the church

59
00:08:24,085 --> 00:08:26,845
operates. Who brought in the flowers?

60
00:08:27,100 --> 00:08:31,365
ANN CONNOR: Was there a special committee?

61
00:08:31,375 --> 00:08:35,765
EDNA: I don't think they had a special committee, as long as I know of.

62
00:08:35,765 --> 00:08:45,965
They may have after the new church was built, but other than that, why, I think the flowers were furnished by different

63
00:08:45,965 --> 00:08:48,625
ones bringing from their gardens.

64
00:08:48,635 --> 00:08:57,405
ANN CONNOR: Yes. One thing that I asked to have done at church on Sunday was to ring the passing bell.

65
00:08:58,400 --> 00:09:05,025
ANN CONNOR: Do you remember having heard the passing bell, and when was it rung?

66
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:07,945
EDNA: What do you mean?

67
00:09:07,955 --> 00:09:15,225
ANN CONNOR: Well, as they pass along the aisle. No, no, no. The passing bell was when someone died and the bell was rung.

68
00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:20,205
EDNA: Oh, that means tolling the bell. Okay, that's a different term.

69
00:09:21,300 --> 00:09:22,865
ANN CONNOR: When did they toll it?

70
00:09:24,400 --> 00:09:31,925
EDNA: Well, when they most surely, if they were brought to the church. I don't remember that being done at Bethel.

71
00:09:31,925 --> 00:09:42,785
But I was one that was down the river road. But I don't know, I don't go in for that, because that

72
00:09:42,785 --> 00:09:46,545
goes through me like, I couldn't stand that.

73
00:09:46,900 --> 00:10:10,745
EDNA: Now, when Uncle Al was buried, he was buried in a, oh, it's Allegheny Cemetery, but it's on the verge of, it's

74
00:10:10,925 --> 00:10:14,425
way out.

75
00:10:15,500 --> 00:10:16,605
ANN CONNOR: What's on the north side?

76
00:10:16,615 --> 00:10:23,605
EDNA: No, it's farther away than that. It's pretty near Butler County.

77
00:10:23,615 --> 00:10:24,945
ANN CONNOR: Wow.

78
00:10:24,955 --> 00:10:40,905
EDNA: And they told that they'll end up for a while there. And they also have the record of hymns that they sang,

79
00:10:41,005 --> 00:10:54,505
that they played, when the funeral procession came into the cemetery.

80
00:10:54,515 --> 00:11:03,365
ANN CONNOR: Well, what do you remember about Edna in connection with the church? Now, you mentioned that she was involved in the play

81
00:11:03,365 --> 00:11:04,865
for the missionaries inside.

82
00:11:09,600 --> 00:11:13,005
ANN CONNOR: What else do you remember that she was active in?

83
00:11:13,900 --> 00:11:15,225
EDNA: Ladies Aid.

84
00:11:15,235 --> 00:11:15,735
ANN CONNOR: So, Ladies Aid.

85
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:22,945
EDNA: I was not a member of that. That was the one that helped to raise money for the missionaries.

86
00:11:22,945 --> 00:11:34,605
Yeah, Reverend Johnston, yeah, in Africa. Then they all done other things for Bethel, the Ladies Aid.

87
00:11:34,605 --> 00:11:43,985
I wasn't a member, but I helped serve tables at their dinner.

88
00:12:07,600 --> 00:12:12,365
EDNA: Dinner.

89
00:12:12,375 --> 00:12:17,345
ANN CONNOR: Did you go to a different school than Edna went to?

90
00:12:18,200 --> 00:12:21,485
ANN CONNOR: Yes, you did. What did you do, go to Croco school?

91
00:12:22,200 --> 00:12:22,685
EDNA: No.

92
00:12:22,900 --> 00:12:25,725
ANN CONNOR: Oh, you went to King's school.

93
00:12:25,735 --> 00:12:31,665
EDNA: King's school and Bethel grade school, the 7th and 8th grade.

94
00:12:32,700 --> 00:12:36,945
ANN CONNOR: Now, when you were going, where was the 7th and 8th grade? Where were they?

95
00:12:39,400 --> 00:12:51,745
EDNA: They were in the seventh grade where I went, was in where they have the arts and crafts center.

96
00:12:54,400 --> 00:13:00,605
ANN CONNOR: And Edna would have gone to Wilson. She went to Wilson.

97
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:13,145
ANN CONNOR: She really wasn't in Bethel. She was in what is now South Park. Yeah, Snowden.

98
00:13:13,305 --> 00:13:15,505
It was Snowden at that time.

99
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:24,625
ANN CONNOR: And then she taught school.

100
00:13:24,635 --> 00:13:34,325
EDNA: Yes. Now, I think I heard them saying over there that night that she taught in, uh, Cur...

101
00:13:35,500 --> 00:13:37,500
ANN CONNOR: Mm-hmm.

102
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:43,285
EDNA: Now, I couldn't tell you what school she taught at, because...

103
00:13:56,700 --> 00:14:07,195
ANN CONNOR: Well, when did you first know Edna in connection with Bethel Church? Did Edna always go to Bethel Church?

104
00:14:08,400 --> 00:14:20,415
EDNA: Now, I might give you some information. She married Rowan Maits, but Rowan Maits was never allowed to join Bethel Church.

105
00:14:20,415 --> 00:14:33,435
His mother never allowed him to join Bethel Church, because she didn't believe in some of the things that the Presbyterians did,

106
00:14:33,435 --> 00:14:42,775
and she was a Baptist, she belonged to Baptists. Edna used to belong to the Baptist church too, and then she turned,

107
00:14:42,775 --> 00:14:58,795
and I guess the whole family joined Bethel, and he was never allowed, his mother was never allowed him to.

108
00:14:59,695 --> 00:15:08,895
Joined Bethel Church. He was officer in Bethel, but he wasn't a member of Bethel.

109
00:15:08,905 --> 00:15:18,815
ANN CONNOR: Well, I remember Edna telling me that oftentimes during the summer they went to a Methodist church that was up on the

110
00:15:18,815 --> 00:15:27,515
hill from where they were, and I laughed at the time, and I said, you were a summer Methodist and a winter

111
00:15:27,515 --> 00:15:38,915
Presbyterian, and she said, oh no, she said, my mother was a Baptist, and sometimes she attended the Baptist church, you know.

112
00:15:38,915 --> 00:15:45,795
I guess it wasn't in the early time of her life, so she went to several different, yeah, different churches.

113
00:15:45,805 --> 00:15:51,735
ANN CONNOR: And then she mentioned that they used to have what they called, well, the Methodist church.

114
00:15:51,735 --> 00:15:58,975
Did she say whether that was Gill Hall? I think that's the one she was referring to, because she pointed up the

115
00:15:58,985 --> 00:16:09,515
hill and we were down in the valley there trying to find the old Cochran Mill when she mentioned they attended the

116
00:16:09,515 --> 00:16:15,275
Methodist Church. So that's one of the older things that says Gill Hall Methodist Church.

117
00:16:15,555 --> 00:16:17,595
That's what I thought was rather interesting.

118
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:25,855
ANN CONNOR: And she mentioned also that in addition to the church attendance, they have what they call a cottage prayer meeting.

119
00:16:25,855 --> 00:16:29,115
Were you involved in any of that type of thing?

120
00:16:29,125 --> 00:16:39,015
EDNA: I used to go to a prayer meeting with Daddy, and leave it over to this old man's one night.

121
00:16:39,615 --> 00:16:53,315
And Daddy had been working pretty hard, and he stopped, and when he picked the Bible up, he got a Catholic Bible

122
00:16:53,315 --> 00:17:05,615
from sending a coupon in from the morning paper, what's it? Something like that, yeah.

123
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:20,575
EDNA: And here he picks this Catholic Bible up, and when he got over to the Miller homestead, why, Reverend Reiter noticed him

124
00:17:20,575 --> 00:17:30,535
going through it and going through it. He says, what's the matter, Ed? Daddy says, I can't find in the Catholic Bible,

125
00:17:30,535 --> 00:17:42,395
there's four kings. And in our Bible there's, there's, I think it's Samuel, and then there's two kings.

126
00:17:42,395 --> 00:17:51,355
So he was having trouble finding what he was looking for. It was supposed to be the Sunday school lesson that they

127
00:17:51,835 --> 00:17:59,255
most generally had at the prayer meetings. And he couldn't find it.

128
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:07,945
ANN CONNOR: Well, that's interesting. I didn't realize that. But I would guess that since the cottage prayer meetings were held in each other's

129
00:18:07,945 --> 00:18:10,645
homes, that the Millers would have been a part of that.

130
00:18:16,200 --> 00:18:18,200
ANN CONNOR: And was that during the week that that was held?

131
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:21,380
EDNA: It was almost certainly a Wednesday evening.

132
00:18:21,400 --> 00:18:22,965
ANN CONNOR: A Wednesday evening.

133
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:25,105
EDNA: A Wednesday evening.

134
00:18:25,115 --> 00:18:25,615
ANN CONNOR: And what kind of things were done in the prayer?

135
00:18:27,700 --> 00:18:32,505
EDNA: Well, just read the Scripture and had prayer.

136
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:38,025
ANN CONNOR: Was there any kind of a discussion?

137
00:18:38,035 --> 00:18:46,145
EDNA: Well, they discussed the Sunday school lesson.

138
00:18:49,200 --> 00:18:55,785
ANN CONNOR: And this, according to Edna, the prayer meetings that she attended were attended by neighbors.

139
00:18:55,785 --> 00:18:59,805
It doesn't make any difference whether you are a Baptist or a Methodist or whatever.

140
00:18:59,815 --> 00:19:06,765
EDNA: Well, we had in our place, why, we most generally ask Mr. and Mrs. Boyer,

141
00:19:06,765 --> 00:19:19,705
and several other ones, your neighbors, neighbors. And and this would be largely because of the distance that would have

142
00:19:19,705 --> 00:19:20,885
to be traveling.

143
00:19:20,900 --> 00:19:28,465
ANN CONNOR: You sort of, it was localized within the areas that was easier to get to.

144
00:19:28,465 --> 00:19:34,325
That's very interesting, for today we don't think that it's any problem to hop in our car and travel.

145
00:19:34,335 --> 00:19:39,165
ANN CONNOR: Though when the weather would be bad, or were these generally in the evening?

146
00:19:39,175 --> 00:19:40,085
EDNA: They were in the evening.

147
00:19:40,095 --> 00:19:44,145
ANN CONNOR: So this again would be, you wouldn't want to be out too late after dark.

148
00:19:48,300 --> 00:19:53,005
ANN CONNOR: That's a whole different way of doing.

149
00:19:53,015 --> 00:20:02,585
ANN CONNOR: And I didn't hear Edna ever doing this, but Ida and Albert told me, when I took care of them, that they

150
00:20:02,585 --> 00:20:17,465
walked in bare feet from the Stone Manse to Bethel Church, and they didn't say anything about putting stockings on or anything.

151
00:20:17,465 --> 00:20:23,505
They just said about putting their shoes on before they go in.

152
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:26,000
EDNA: Yeah.

153
00:20:26,400 --> 00:20:32,405
ANN CONNOR: Now, how many in Bethel Church would do that today?

154
00:20:32,415 --> 00:20:38,385
EDNA: Not, I can't think of anybody at this point. I can't think of anybody at this point.

155
00:20:39,700 --> 00:20:47,125
ANN CONNOR: Well, I'm trying to remember, you know, one of the things that I think is so interesting about the early history was

156
00:20:47,125 --> 00:20:51,005
the fact that they had to depend on either walking or being by horseback.

157
00:20:51,005 --> 00:20:55,205
Did you, when you came to church, did you come in a buggy?

158
00:20:55,215 --> 00:21:02,865
EDNA: Well, we, uh, towards the last, my, uh, Mr., um, Poellot, uh, John L.

159
00:21:02,865 --> 00:21:21,225
Poellot, had the wagon shop in Sodom, and he made, he built surreys, and the two surreys were just alike.

160
00:21:22,500 --> 00:21:32,985
EDNA: And Daddy used to devil, uh, one Sunday Grandma Wilson came out and she didn't look where she was going and she

161
00:21:32,985 --> 00:21:45,725
started to get into Mrs. Phillips' surrey, and Daddy, of course, with him being as devilish as he was, he let her

162
00:21:45,725 --> 00:21:49,145
do it, and then he deviled her afterwards.

163
00:21:51,600 --> 00:21:56,105
ANN CONNOR: It's like getting into the wrong car.

164
00:21:56,115 --> 00:22:03,965
ANN CONNOR: Well, now you mentioned Sodom. Where was Sodom, and how did it get its name?

165
00:22:03,975 --> 00:22:17,625
EDNA: I don't know how it got its name, but it was located down where the 19 goes across, down there below.

166
00:22:19,400 --> 00:22:37,365
EDNA: Well, below where George Walters and Mary Walters live, and where that, down in that area there, where you go underneath Route

167
00:22:37,365 --> 00:22:44,125
19 now, where McMurray Road goes on to McLaughlin Run Road.

168
00:22:44,135 --> 00:22:51,085
ANN CONNOR: Yeah, I see. So that was, yeah.

169
00:22:51,095 --> 00:22:58,485
EDNA: Well, there must be a reason why it's got that terrible name.

170
00:22:58,495 --> 00:23:03,665
ANN CONNOR: Well, I think that was one of the things that I think about when I think of Mrs.

171
00:23:03,665 --> 00:23:13,225
Maits, and you too, that you remember the, actually, the third meeting house. Were you there when they took it down?

172
00:23:13,385 --> 00:23:17,765
Do you remember what the process was, ripping it all down?

173
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:18,925
EDNA: No.

174
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:22,000
ANN CONNOR: Too bad.

175
00:23:22,200 --> 00:23:36,585
EDNA: See, I was only about two years old when they had that wind and took one side of the roof off.

176
00:23:36,585 --> 00:23:54,925
What Daddy talked about, they had four, um, you know, there's a picture in here, they had four chandeliers or lamps, oil

177
00:23:54,935 --> 00:24:13,215
lamps, and he noticed them going up, they were fastened onto the rafters, and when that went up, when the wind would

178
00:24:13,215 --> 00:24:18,915
get under that part of the roof, they would go up to the ceiling, and then they'd come back down.

179
00:24:18,915 --> 00:24:39,755
And that's when Daddy said that he thought the church was haunted. He always had his way of seeing the funny side

180
00:24:39,755 --> 00:24:42,415
of everything.

181
00:24:42,425 --> 00:24:51,935
ANN CONNOR: A sense of humor.

182
00:24:52,700 --> 00:24:57,515
ANN CONNOR: No, I didn't know that Edna was born over there in that house.

183
00:24:58,000 --> 00:25:06,535
EDNA: Well, she told me that she was born not in the house, but a log house, just down from where that house

184
00:25:06,535 --> 00:25:20,135
was. And see, Grandma Wilson raised another girl. She was never, they never adopted her.

185
00:25:20,145 --> 00:25:35,815
EDNA: But you'd look through books of Grandma Wilson's in the cupboard and you'd find Nellie Beam.

186
00:25:35,815 --> 00:25:50,875
Now, uh, Nellie Beam, her husband, her dad drank so, and, uh, different things, and so they took the girl off of

187
00:25:50,875 --> 00:26:08,985
them, and Grandma Wilson, uh, put her to old school in Pittsburgh, Academy, I think they called it, but she was never

188
00:26:08,985 --> 00:26:17,005
adopted, and she married down a little.

189
00:26:17,015 --> 00:26:25,665
EDNA: Ed, um, Ed, um, Smith.

190
00:26:29,700 --> 00:26:33,285
ANN CONNOR: From down in Capitana?

191
00:26:33,295 --> 00:26:44,185
EDNA: No, that is from...

192
00:26:46,100 --> 00:26:50,225
ANN CONNOR: In recent years, you've kind of kept in touch with Edna by telephone, haven't you?

193
00:26:50,235 --> 00:26:52,645
EDNA: Oh, yes.

194
00:26:57,300 --> 00:27:06,525
EDNA: She got the morning paper, and I didn't get the paper, and she noticed the death notice when she called me.

195
00:27:07,400 --> 00:27:09,265
EDNA: Keep in touch on that, hon.

196
00:27:12,600 --> 00:27:19,085
